@page "/projects"

<PageTitle>Projects | Aetheric Forge</PageTitle>

<div class="projects-page">
    <header class="projects-hero">
        <p class="projects-hero__eyebrow">Projects and Initiatives</p>
        <h1>Ideas become useful when they survive contact with reality.</h1>
        <p class="projects-hero__lede">
            Aetheric Forge projects are working systems, reference designs, and learning
            environments. Each one is built in the open so the decisions, trade-offs,
            and occasional scars remain available to the next person solving the problem.
        </p>
        <a class="projects-hero__action"
           href="https://github.com/aetheric-forge"
           target="_blank"
           rel="noreferrer">
            Browse all repositories
        </a>
    </header>

    <main class="projects-list" aria-label="Aetheric Forge projects">
        <article id="aetheric-runtime" class="project">
            <div class="project__number" aria-hidden="true">01</div>
            <div class="project__body">
                <div class="project__meta">
                    <span class="project__status">Active development</span>
                    <span>Software architecture</span>
                </div>
                <h2>Aetheric Runtime</h2>
                <p class="project__summary">
                    A modular foundation for composing institutions: software systems whose
                    services, authority, knowledge, identity, and communication reflect the
                    organization they support.
                </p>
                <p>
                    The Runtime explores a more deliberate alternative to accumulating
                    disconnected applications. Its abstractions cover capabilities such as
                    archives, libraries, registries, identity, and message exchange, while
                    institution packages compose those capabilities into a coherent operating
                    environment. The result is both usable code and a reference architecture
                    for reasoning about long-lived organizational systems.
                </p>
                <a class="project__link"
                   href="https://github.com/aetheric-forge/aetheric-runtime"
                   target="_blank"
                   rel="noreferrer">
                    Explore Aetheric Runtime on GitHub →
                </a>
            </div>
        </article>

        <article class="project">
            <div class="project__number" aria-hidden="true">02</div>
            <div class="project__body">
                <div class="project__meta">
                    <span class="project__status">Early construction</span>
                    <span>Learning and collaboration</span>
                </div>
                <h2>Forge Campus</h2>
                <p class="project__summary">
                    A learning and collaboration institution where people can develop real
                    capability by participating in real projects.
                </p>
                <p>
                    Forge Campus is the first institution composed on the Aetheric Runtime.
                    It brings the architectural work into direct contact with education:
                    membership, workshops, shared knowledge, durable project artifacts, and
                    collaboration all become parts of the same environment. It is intended to
                    support mentorship and practical experimentation without reducing either
                    one to a conventional course-management system.
                </p>
                <a class="project__link" href="/campus/apply">
                    Learn about joining Forge Campus →
                </a>
            </div>
        </article>

        <article class="project">
            <div class="project__number" aria-hidden="true">03</div>
            <div class="project__body">
                <div class="project__meta">
                    <span class="project__status">Online now</span>
                    <span>Open infrastructure</span>
                </div>
                <h2>Aetheric Web</h2>
                <p class="project__summary">
                    The public face of the initiative—and a proving ground for the platform
                    beneath it.
                </p>
                <p>
                    This site communicates the work, hosts the emerging Campus experience,
                    and exercises the Runtime in a deployed application. Its source remains
                    public so the website itself can serve as a practical example of how the
                    pieces fit together, from interface and application design through to
                    operation in production.
                </p>
                <a class="project__link"
                   href="https://github.com/aetheric-forge/aetheric-web"
                   target="_blank"
                   rel="noreferrer">
                    Explore Aetheric Web on GitHub →
                </a>
            </div>
        </article>
    </main>

    <section class="projects-invitation" aria-labelledby="projects-invitation-title">
        <div>
            <p class="projects-invitation__eyebrow">Open by design</p>
            <h2 id="projects-invitation-title">Follow the work—or help shape it.</h2>
            <p>
                The repositories are public because the process is part of the product.
                Explore the code, raise a question, or join the Campus as it takes form.
            </p>
        </div>
        <div class="projects-invitation__actions">
            <a class="projects-invitation__primary" href="https://github.com/aetheric-forge" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Visit GitHub</a>
            <a class="projects-invitation__secondary" href="/campus/apply">Join Campus</a>
        </div>
    </section>

    <Footer />
</div>
